{"annotations":[
  {"sentence":"Increased use of AI in our offerings and internal systems may create new avenues of abuse for bad actors.","kind":"Risk","category":"Sociotechnical","subcategory":"Malicious Actors / Misuse","strength":null},
  {"sentence":"The costs of compliance with these measures are high and are likely to increase in the future, including as a result of differing, and sometimes conflicting, laws and regulations.","kind":"Risk","category":"Legal","subcategory":"Compliance Costs","strength":null},
  {"sentence":"•AI: Laws and regulations focused on the development, use, and provision of AI technologies and other digital products and services, which could result in monetary penalties or other regulatory actions.","kind":"Risk","category":"Legal","subcategory":"Uncertainty & Complexity","strength":null},
  {"sentence":"The EU AI Act introduces various requirements for AI systems and models placed on the market or put into service in the EU, including specific transparency and other requirements for general purpose AI systems and the models on which those systems are based.","kind":"Risk","category":"Legal","subcategory":"Compliance Costs","strength":null},
  {"sentence":"In the U.S., there is increasing uncertainty as to the federal government's approach to AI regulation going forward, as the continued applicability of the White House's 2023 Executive Order on the Safe, Secure, and Trustworthy Development and Use of Artificial Intelligence, which lays out a framework for the U.S. government, among other things, to monitor private sector development of certain foundation models, remains subject to regulatory development.","kind":"Risk","category":"Legal","subcategory":"Uncertainty & Complexity","strength":null},
  {"sentence":"Several states are considering enacting or have already enacted regulations concerning the use of AI technologies, including those focused on consumer protection, and depending on the scope of AI regulation at the federal level, some states may move to regulate AI model development and deployment.","kind":"Risk","category":"Legal","subcategory":"Uncertainty & Complexity","strength":null}
]}
